in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic/eigenform

# @epistemologic/cybernetic/distinction — Spencer-Brown's mark of
# distinction; the FLOOR of the @cyberpunk family. Spencer-Brown 1969
# (*Laws of Form*, chapters 1-10 and 11). The most foundational of the
# cybernetic substrate-properties: every higher-altitude distinction
# the substrate makes presupposes the mark this property declares.
#
# Per §8.8 of the recursion-lock-tower audit, distinction is the
# eighth canonical-rep witness and the *floor* of @cyberpunk: Beer's
# VSM presupposes it (pre-VSM altitude); Bateson's hierarchy presupposes
# it (type-0 ↔ the act-of-making-a-distinction); second_order observes
# what distinction marks. The family is bottomed at distinction AND
# topped at second_order — finite altitude range, well-defined bundle
# holonomy (candidate recognition #66).
#
# === The Spencer-Brown claim, verbatim ===
#
# Spencer-Brown, G. (1969). *Laws of Form*. Allen & Unwin. Chapter 1
# (the first canon):
#
#   Draw a distinction. Call it the first distinction. The space
#   thus marked off has two sides — the marked state and the
#   unmarked state. The mark of distinction IS the boundary; the
#   sides are what the boundary separates.
#
# Chapter 11 (the re-entry canon):
#
#   A mark may re-enter its own indicational space. The form that
#   results IS a fixed point of the recursive substitution: f = f(f).
#   Re-entry is the calculus's bridge from the propositional to the
#   imaginary; from finite combinatorics to recursive identity.
#
# === Why this is the floor ===
#
# Per §8.8 (Reads A, B, C held + Read D dissolved + Read E held at
# maximum density):
#
# - Read A (mark ↔ distinction-space) HELD; τ = Spencer-Brown cross
#   with condensation + cancellation axioms.
# - Read B (marked ↔ unmarked) HELD as value-level restriction of A.
# - Read C (canonical ρ) HELD at FREE BOOLEAN ALGEBRA on one generator
#   acting on V_distinction = Mark ⊕ DistinctionSpace. The C.2 choice
#   over C.1 (two-element) and C.3 (Heyting) is forced by Spencer-Brown
#   ch.1-10 BEING the free algebra; C.1 collapses operation-level to
#   value-level; C.3 is what transparency<p> reads at HIGHER altitudes,
#   not the floor.
# - Read D (form refusal — re-entry) REFUSED: re-entry IS eigenform
#   (recognition #38). One ancestor (eigenform), two inheritors
#   (distinction at the floor, second_order at the top). Inherited
#   from @epistemologic/cybernetic/eigenform via the `in` clause above;
#   not restated here.
# - Read E (substrate-already-had-the-word) HELD at MAXIMUM DENSITY
#   (19 instances, densest in the cascade; cf. autopoiesis 13,
#   second_order 14, bateson_learning 9). Maximum density at the floor
#   is structurally consistent: every higher altitude's distinctions
#   originate here.
#
# Fourth canonical-rep species in the recursion-lock tower:
#
#   species            ρ choice                       ancestry
#   ------------------ ----------------------------- ---------------------
#   autopoiesis         adjoint rep on G              G's self-action
#   bateson_learning    graded rep on ⊕_N V_N        RW + Kac
#   second_order        regular rep on L²(𝒢)        von Foerster + Peter-Weyl
#   distinction         free Boolean algebra rep      Spencer-Brown ch.1-10
#
# Each ρ forced by mathematical ancestry; no ad-hoc choices.
#
# === Why eigenform inheritance, not re-statement ===
#
# Per §8.8.1 (the eigenform-precedence question): re-entry IS
# eigenform; the reflexive turn IS eigenform; one ancestor, two
# inheritors. This shard declares `in @epistemologic/cybernetic/eigenform`
# above so the fixed-point machinery (fixed_point, is_fixed_point,
# identity_from_fixed, eigenform_witnessing) is inherited rather than
# restated. The species-specific contribution at this altitude is
# the mark and the distinction-space; the recursion that closes via
# re-entry is eigenform's already-declared machinery instantiated at
# the mark.
#
# Forward-promised: when a consumer pulls the re-entry verification,
# the discharge IS `eigenform_witnessing(reentry_carrier)` with the
# carrier's seed = mark, iteration = cross, witness = the re-entered
# mark satisfying mark = cross(mark, distinction_space(mark)).
#
# === The verifiable shape ===
#
# - Declares the carrier of a distinction: mark, distinction_space,
#   cross. The cross IS Spencer-Brown's primitive operation.
# - Declares the two value-level operations (marked_state,
#   unmarked_state) as the verdict surface at the species boundary.
# - Declares the inheritance interface to eigenform: reentry_as_eigenform
#   names the recursion's fixed-point carrier so consumers can compose
#   with eigenform_witnessing without restating the obligation.
# - Verifiable at the @code/metalogue/materialize.classify boundary via
#   the same transparency<p> discriminator surface variety and eigenform
#   use; the loss profile (what the cross dropped) recoverable from
#   the opacity_map per @glass.
#
# === The 4-way bilateral mapping ===
#
# Per the cybernetic foundation §4.1, distinction's property/operation
# seam maps to four cybernetic distinctions simultaneously:
#
# - Spencer-Brown's mark/unmarked: the mark IS the property's load-
#   bearing carrier; the unmarked state IS the complement at the
#   distinction-space.
# - von Foerster's observer/observed: the mark IS what the observer
#   draws; the distinction-space IS the observed; second_order
#   reflects on this distinction to land at its eigenform.
# - Maturana's structure/organisation: the mark IS the operational
#   closure that makes the autopoietic system distinguishable from
#   its medium; without distinction, no autopoietic identity.
# - Bateson's information-as-difference: "the difference that makes
#   a difference" Bateson 1972 IS Spencer-Brown's mark lifted to the
#   epistemic altitude. Bateson's hierarchy of logical types builds
#   on the type-0 act-of-distinction.
#
# Four traditions converging at one carrier. The substrate runs all
# four at once at the floor altitude.
#
# === No operational sibling THIS tick ===
#
# Per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] no `@mirror/cybernetics/distinction`
# operational sibling lands at this tick. The substrate ALREADY has
# the operational machinery (every property declaration at every
# altitude IS an instance of the mark operation; every type-system
# discriminator IS a distinction); the property at this altitude
# names the carrier so downstream shards can declare
# `requires distinction_well_formed(my_carrier)` rather than restate
# the mark obligation in each species.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   the mark of distinction     Spencer-Brown 1969 (Laws of Form),
#                               chapters 1-10. The original. The
#                               propositional substructure of every
#                               species' rep (§18.1 of the recursion-
#                               lock-tower audit).
#   re-entry                    Spencer-Brown 1969 (Laws of Form),
#                               chapter 11. The reflexive turn.
#                               Inherited from
#                               @epistemologic/cybernetic/eigenform.
#   information-as-difference   Bateson 1972 (*Steps to an Ecology
#                               of Mind*). "The difference that
#                               makes a difference" — Spencer-Brown's
#                               mark at the epistemic altitude.
#   free Boolean algebra        Halmos 1963 (*Lectures on Boolean
#                               Algebras*). The canonical algebraic
#                               representation of distinction at the
#                               propositional layer. The substrate's
#                               ρ choice is Halmos's free algebra on
#                               one generator.
#   second-order observation    von Foerster 1981 (*Observing
#                               Systems*). The observer that observes
#                               distinction-making is the canonical
#                               consumer of this property at the
#                               second_order altitude (§8.8.1: the
#                               two inheritors of eigenform).
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word cross-references (5 of 19) ===
#
# Per §8.8 Read E, distinction sits at maximum density (19 instances).
# Five named explicitly here as the load-bearing cross-references; the
# remaining 14 land in the spec's §10 and propagate via consumer pulls
# at higher altitudes:
#
# 1. The mark IS the type-system discriminator. Every `type T = | a | b`
#    declaration in the substrate IS Spencer-Brown's mark applied to
#    the value-space; the variants are the marked states, the
#    complement is the unmarked. See [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-
#    everything]] (typed lambdas as marked-state declarations).
# 2. The mark IS the `transparency<p>` discriminator. The success /
#    partial(opacity_map) / failure(opacity_map) trichotomy IS three
#    marked states over the verdict-space. See [[architecture-glass-
#    wall-substrate-types]] (Imperfect + Transparency as substrate
#    vocabulary; the species realisation of distinction's verdict).
# 3. The mark IS the @glass species boundary. The recognitive
#    discriminator at the species transition (@code/metalogue/materialize
#    .classify) IS the substrate's load-bearing distinction operation —
#    the mark applied to the cross-species projection. See
#    [[architecture-splinter-and-spectral-db-edges]] (K_n via OID-graph
#    is the distinction at the floor of fragmentation).
# 4. The mark IS the variety axis. Every per-axis budget in
#    @epistemologic/cybernetic/variety IS a distinction over the
#    state-space; the variety vector IS the multiset of distinctions
#    a shard declares it can make. See [[architecture-ashby-multi-
#    dimensional-variety]] (variety as vector of distinctions across
#    five axes).
# 5. The mark IS the form/process partition (recognition #55).
#    @mirror (state-observation) ↔ @kintsugi (transformation-engine)
#    IS Spencer-Brown's first distinction at family-root altitude;
#    the partition IS the mark drawn at the cybernetic family
#    boundary. See [[architecture-form-process-partition-at-family-
#    root]] (form/process at family-root; distinction at family-floor;
#    same mark, two altitudes).
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/cyberpunk-distinction.md (Mara's canonical
#               spec, commit `96906e2`, mara/cyberpunk-distinction-spec
#               branch, 916 lines, the source of this shard);
#               docs/math/the-tower/recursion-locks.md §8.8 (witness;
#               canonical ρ; fourth canonical-rep species),
#               §8.8.1 (eigenform precedence; inheritance from
#               @epistemologic/cybernetic/eigenform),
#               §18.1 (distinction provides the propositional
#               sub-algebra of every species' rep),
#               §19.4 (substrate-landing path item 3; this shard).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-glass-wall-substrate-types]],
#                      [[architecture-form-process-partition-at-family-
#                       root]] (distinction at family-floor; same mark
#                       as the family-root partition, two altitudes),
#                      [[architecture-ashby-multi-dimensional-variety]]
#                       (variety vector IS multiset of distinctions),
#                      [[architecture-bateson-form-behaviour-partition]]
#                       (Bateson's form/substance IS distinction
#                       applied at substrate/@io boundary),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (mark, distinction-
#                       space, cross are typed carriers; no bare
#                       references),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                       (densest single species at 19 instances;
#                       maximum density at the floor altitude is
#                       structurally consistent).
# Related shards: epistemologic/cybernetic.mirror (the family root),
#                 epistemologic/cybernetic/eigenform.mirror (the
#                  ancestor inherited via `in`; provides fixed_point
#                  carrier + eigenform_witnessing predicate that
#                  reentry_as_eigenform threads through),
#                 epistemologic/cybernetic/variety.mirror (the
#                  precedent species; same shape; variety's per-axis
#                  budget IS distinction at each axis),
#                 glass.mirror (the @glass altitude this property's
#                  verdicts surface against; `transparency<p>` IS the
#                  verdict-space's mark over success / partial / failure).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/epistemologic/cybernetic/distinction.mirror` declares
# `@epistemologic/cybernetic/distinction` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.
#
# Per §19.2 path-migration dependency: this shard lands at the
# current-main path `@epistemologic/cybernetic/distinction`. When the
# @cyberpunk family-root migration merges to main (Taut's
# `taut/t11-11-cybernetic-coherence-benchmark`), this shard relocates
# via `git mv` to `shards/cyberpunk/distinction.mirror`. The forward-
# promised path is on the audit's §19.4 substrate-landing sequence,
# item 3.

source @arxiv/cybernetics/spencer-brown-1969
source @arxiv/cybernetics/bateson-1972
source @arxiv/algebra/halmos-1963

# === The mark carrier ===
#
# A typed reference per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] naming Spencer-Brown's
# load-bearing primitive: the mark of distinction. The mark IS the
# boundary the calculus draws; the value of this carrier IS the act of
# making a distinction lifted to substrate vocabulary.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref. Two marks
# with byte-equal underlying references ARE the same mark under the
# substrate's content-addressing.
type mark = ref

# === The distinction-space carrier ===
#
# The space within which a mark draws its boundary. Per Spencer-Brown
# ch.1, every mark presupposes a space the mark partitions; the
# distinction-space IS that space. The mark and the distinction-space
# are dual carriers: a mark without a space is ill-formed; a space
# without a mark is the unmarked state at the family-root altitude.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type distinction_space = ref

# === The cross operation ===
#
# Spencer-Brown's primitive: cross takes a mark and a distinction-space
# and returns the distinction-space transformed by the mark's boundary.
# Per Spencer-Brown ch.2 (the condensation axiom), repeated cross
# operations on the same mark in the same space condense to a single
# application; per ch.3 (the cancellation axiom), a cross followed by
# its inverse cancels.
#
# The cross IS τ for Read A: the natural substitution between mark
# and distinction-space at the species boundary. See §8.8 Read A held
# via Spencer-Brown cross with condensation + cancellation axioms.
type cross_op = mark -> distinction_space

# === The two value-level operations ===
#
# Read B held as value-level restriction of A: marked_state and
# unmarked_state are the two verdicts the mark surfaces at any point
# within the distinction-space. The verdict carrier IS the substrate's
# existing `verdict` family (success / partial / failure); the species
# realisation interprets the verdict per Spencer-Brown's two-state
# semantics.
#
# Body discharges per-species at the realisation boundary. Same shape
# as the four metalogue shims at `shards/code/metalogue.mirror`: the
# substrate declares the obligation; species bodies discharge when a
# consumer pulls.
marked_state(s: distinction_space) -> verdict { \ }
unmarked_state(s: distinction_space) -> verdict { \ }

# === The cross operator (Spencer-Brown's primitive) ===
#
# Applies the mark to the distinction-space, returning the space
# transformed by the boundary the mark draws. The condensation and
# cancellation axioms are substrate-fact at the realisation boundary;
# the action body discharges per-species.
#
# Body shape: `\` per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]; the discharge IS
# the species-specific instantiation of Spencer-Brown's primitive.
cross(m: mark, s: distinction_space) -> distinction_space { \ }

# === The inheritance from eigenform ===
#
# Per §8.8 Read D dissolution: re-entry IS eigenform. Per §8.8.1: one
# ancestor (eigenform), two inheritors (distinction at the floor,
# second_order at the top). This shard declares the inheritance
# interface here: reentry_as_eigenform names the carrier the consumer
# threads through eigenform_witnessing without restating the fixed-
# point obligation at this altitude.
#
# The carrier's structure: seed = mark, iteration = cross over the
# distinction-space, witness = the re-entered mark satisfying
# mark = cross(mark, distinction_space(mark)). This IS Spencer-Brown's
# ch.11 re-entry canon lifted to eigenform's fixed_point carrier:
# f = f(f) becomes mark = cross(mark, distinction_space(mark)).
#
# Returns `fixed_point<mark>`: the eigenform whose witness IS the
# mark that re-enters its own indicational space. Downstream
# consumers compose with eigenform_witnessing(carrier) to verify
# convergence; the body here threads the mark into the carrier per
# species realisation.
#
# This action IS the bridge the substrate uses to avoid restating
# fixed-point machinery at the distinction altitude. Per
# [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]] (densest density at
# the floor altitude): the fixed-point obligation already lives at
# eigenform; distinction names HOW the mark becomes the eigenform's
# witness via re-entry.
reentry_as_eigenform(m: mark) -> fixed_point(mark) { \ }

# === distinction_well_formed — the bilateral verdict predicate ===
#
# `distinction_well_formed(carrier)` is the predicate consumer shards
# name in a `requires` clause to declare bilateral agreement (per
# recognition #37, the Pask-agreement reading of `requires`) that the
# (mark, distinction_space) pair they hold IS a well-formed Spencer-Brown
# distinction — i.e. cross satisfies condensation + cancellation; the
# marked_state and unmarked_state verdicts partition the distinction-
# space without remainder.
#
# The bilateral commitment: the carrier commits to declaring the pair
# (mark, distinction_space); the consumer commits to discharging the
# verification at the species boundary.
#
# Declared as a typed predicate so downstream species shards can
# write `requires distinction_well_formed(my_carrier)` — same shape as
# `variety.variety_preserving(species)`,
# `eigenform.eigenform_witnessing(carrier)`, and the metalogue
# `requires substrate_pull_preserving(shim_X)` pattern at
# `shards/code/metalogue.mirror`. The body is `\`; the discharge IS
# the conjunction of (cross axioms + verdict partition) at the
# species boundary.
#
# No `requires distinction_well_formed(…)` clauses are added at THIS
# shard: the property declares the predicate; consumers add the
# clauses when they pull. Per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] the
# operational sibling at `@mirror/cybernetics/distinction` lands the
# same way.
distinction_well_formed(m: mark, s: distinction_space) -> verdict { \ }

out @epistemologic/cybernetic/distinction
out mark
out distinction_space
out cross_op
out marked_state
out unmarked_state
out cross
out reentry_as_eigenform
out distinction_well_formed
